	"lanternwood_debt": {"name": "The Cutters' Debt", "giver": "ebba", "zone": "westreach", "offer": true, "avail": "qd:wr_cold_light",
		"where": "Ebba Sallow, on her punt at Reedholm",
		"text": "Ebba took three cold caps from the Lanternwood to light her punt's bow, and the wood let her. She has been uneasy since. The cutters of the Hollow lived by those caps nine winters, she says, and nobody has paid them for the light. Walk the cutters' route out of the wood, take a cap-lamp from their last stone, carry it the whole way to her landing without letting it die, and decide whose the light is.",
		"steps": [
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(-330.0, -8.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The ring of giant caps",
				"text": "Read the cutters' ring for what the wood was owed ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "ring", "at": Vector2(-332.4, -6.4), "name": "the cutters' ring", "text": "A ring of stumps in the ring of caps, each cut flat and sat upon. Nine of them are worn to a polish. A tenth has never been sat on, and a cap has grown up through the middle of it, pale and exactly as wide as a man."},
					{"key": "tally", "at": Vector2(-330.0, -5.6), "name": "a tally in the bark", "text": "Nine winters of tally on the bark of the largest cap, a stroke a night, in rows of seven. Beside the last row, small: we paid in nothing. The wood let us have the light for nothing. I do not like owing it."},
					{"key": "axe", "at": Vector2(-327.6, -4.8), "name": "a laid-down axe", "text": "An axe laid across two stumps with its edge turned to the cap, not the wood: a cutter's way of saying I will not. The haft is wound with a strip of blue cloth, tied by someone who meant to come back."},
