				"text": "Read the landing for whose the light was ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "punt", "at": Vector2(-340.4, 371.6), "name": "Ebba's punt", "text": "The punt's bow, bare of paint, with a cap-lamp hung in a net. The net's knots are a cutter's, not a fisher's. Somebody taught Ebba to tie them, and she has forgotten who."},
					{"key": "slate", "at": Vector2(-338.0, 372.4), "name": "a slate on the post", "text": "A slate by the landing stairs: OWED TO THE CUTTERS OF THE HOLLOW, ONE LIGHT. Under it, chalked and wiped and chalked: PAID? PAID? Ebba's hand, and, beside it, another, firm: not by you."},
					{"key": "net", "at": Vector2(-335.6, 373.2), "name": "a net of caps", "text": "A net hung to dry on the jetty rail, full of small cold caps, each one a lamp for a boat. Nine winters of them, and a dozen more cutting on the shore, new, green, still dripping the milk of the wood."},
