		"outcome": {"bow": "Ebba touched the cap in her bow with one finger. 'Then I carry it,' she said. 'I would sooner. A debt you hold is a thing you can pay.' She put a second knot in the net, her own, and it was not a cutter's.",
			"shore": "Ebba laughed, a short wet startled sound, and went down on her knees on the jetty to look at the shore. 'Twelve by the morning,' she said. 'A wood on my landing. What will the cutters say?' She did not wait to find out. \"If you are going back by the road,\" she called, \"the stable at Hearthward will lend you a horse, and the Count keeps a Race page for the ones who ride.\"",
			"wood": "'It went home.' Ebba sat on the punt's edge a long time. 'Then there is no debt, and I have been paying nothing for nine winters out of habit.' She looked at her hands. 'I think I should like to be told what to do with them.'",
			"": "The count was left as it was."}},
	"cairn_count": {"name": "The Cairns' Count", "giver": "wat", "zone": "eastreach", "offer": true, "avail": "qd:er_halter_bell",
		"where": "Burl, at the stable in Lastlight",
		"text": "Burl carried Isobel's halter-bell to the rag-pole at the Cairn Tower and the heath answered. He has been thinking about it since. A cairn for every pilgrim who turned back, they say: a thousand of them, and nobody has counted. He asks you to count them, the way the One Who Counted did, and to bring a light back from the tower to Lastlight, and to say what a count is for.",
		"steps": [
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(330.0, 250.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The Counting Cairn",
				"text": "Read the Counting Cairn for how the count began ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "first", "at": Vector2(327.6, 251.6), "name": "the first cairn", "text": "The first cairn is no higher than a table, and has a pebble for each one who set a stone. One. The second cairn has two. The count goes up by the arithmetic of grief: each pilgrim added a stone, and the next added two."},
					{"key": "pole", "at": Vector2(330.0, 252.4), "name": "the rag-pole", "text": "The rag-pole at the tower's foot with its seven bleached rags and a new one, a halter-bell's strap, knotted last. Under it, chalk: SHE ARRIVED. Burl's hand."},
					{"key": "slate", "at": Vector2(332.4, 253.2), "name": "a counter's slate", "text": "A flat stone with tally strokes in rows of nine, ending in a smear where the counter stopped. Under the smear: I COULD NOT COUNT THE LAST. I WILL NOT PRETEND I DID."},
				]},
			{"kind": "tracks", "r": 12.0, "label": "The cairn road",
				"text": "Walk the cairn road south to the Cairn Tower, counting as you go ({n}/{of})",
				"marks": [
					{"at": Vector2(336.0, 272.0), "text": "Cairns on both sides of the track, low, in ranks, and every one with a stone laid on its top by a hand that did not know the one beneath. You count forty. You lose count at forty."},
					{"at": Vector2(342.0, 296.0), "text": "A leaning cairn with a staff driven through it, and a pilgrim's token, a tin Open Door, hung on the staff and turned to face the road, not the mountain."},
					{"at": Vector2(338.0, 318.0), "text": "A cairn built round something: a boot, a good boot, with its laces tied. Somebody sat down here, took the boot off, set it down, and was covered."},
					{"at": Vector2(330.0, 336.0), "text": "The tower's foot. The ranks stop. The ground ahead is clear, swept, and in the middle of it one cairn stands alone, taller than the rest, with a single stone on top and a cold candle stub beside it."},
				]},
			{"kind": "find", "text": "Take a coal from the lamp at the Cairn Tower's foot, in the lantern"},
			{"kind": "lantern_walk", "from": "cairn_count_coal", "to": Vector2(326.0, 62.0), "r": 8.0, "label": "Lastlight's road gate",
				"relight": "Take another coal from the tower's lamp.",
				"arrive": "You set the coal in the road gate's lantern, and the heath, behind you, goes on being a heath. But something in the long dark south of the road, a very long way off, lets out a breath.",
				"text": "Carry the tower's coal north to Lastlight's road gate. Walk it, the whole length of the heath: a run, a roll, a blow or deep water puts it out"},
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(349.0, 60.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The Lamp Tower",
				"text": "Read the Lamp Tower's log for what Lastlight owes the cairns ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "log", "at": Vector2(346.6, 61.6), "name": "the keeper's log", "text": "Isolde's lamp-book, open on its lectern. Sixty years of dusks, each with its weather. On the night of the Night, one word: out. Under it, the next dusk: lit. The lamp lit itself. Isolde never asked why."},
					{"key": "window", "at": Vector2(349.0, 62.4), "name": "a window facing south", "text": "A window cut in the tower facing the heath, wider than the others. A bench under it, worn to the shape of a woman sitting, and a ledge for a cup. From here a keeper could watch the cairns, if she wished."},
					{"key": "count", "at": Vector2(351.4, 63.2), "name": "a count on the wall", "text": "Chalk on the tower's wall, in a child's hand, in nines: Mother Vell's grandson, counting the cairns from the window. His number is higher than the cairns. He counted the stars as well."},
				]},
			{"kind": "vigil", "at": Vector2(349.0, 60.0), "r": 9.0, "time": 60.0, "gloom": 0.6, "label": "The Lamp Tower", "noun": "tower", "prop": "lantern_lit",
				"waves": [{"at": 12.0, "kinds": ["husk"], "n": 2, "say": "The heath's dead come up the road to see who has carried a light to Lastlight."},
					{"at": 28.0, "kinds": ["gaunt"], "n": 3, "say": "A very tall thing stands at the road's edge and does not come closer. It is counting."},
					{"at": 44.0, "kinds": ["husk"], "n": 2, "say": "The tower's flame bends south. The heath leans in."}],
				"held": "The tower's flame stands straight. Somewhere south, the ranks of cairns settle, a thousand small stones at once.", "away": "Go back to the tower. A count is kept at the place it is read.",
				"text": "Keep the cairns' coal beside the tower's flame through the night ({t} s)"},
