		"outcome": {"wick": "Burl stood at the stable door looking south for a long time. 'A lamp in the window,' he said. 'It's the oldest thing a place can do for a traveller.' He went in and sat with the mare, and she nosed at his sleeve, and he let her.",
			"stone": "'The second stone.' Burl turned his cap in his hands. 'I never thought of it. A cairn that is not alone is a cairn with a neighbour. A thing that is counted, and then counted again.' He took the cap back to the stable and hung it on the nail beside the halter.",
			"name": "'Isobel.' Burl said the name twice. 'The mare's, the pilgrim's. That is the right thing to give a heath that counts.' He laughed, to his own surprise. 'I have never been so glad of an easy answer. It is only that nobody had said one yet.'",
			"": "The count was left as it was."}},
	"oak_memory": {"name": "What the Oak Remembers", "giver": "hesper", "zone": "deepsouth", "offer": true, "avail": "qd:ds_door_witch|qd:ds_witchs_price",
		"where": "Hesper Lark, at the farmhouse door in Fallowmere",
		"text": "Hesper's grandmother's grandmother is said to have been born in the shade of the Hollow King, a dead oak forty-four yards high in the Southwood, and Hesper has never seen it. The oak has a hollow, and a hall in it, and something kept there. She wants to know what an oak remembers. Follow the burners' trail from their stack to the oak, read the hall, carry the oak's ember all the way home to the farm, and decide what to do with a memory that big.",
		"steps": [
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(130.0, 330.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The burners' ruin",
				"text": "Read the burners' ruin for the way to the oak ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "clamp", "at": Vector2(127.6, 331.6), "name": "a cold clamp", "text": "A clamp that was never drawn. Nine winters of turf have grown over the charcoal inside it and the whole mound is a green hill with a warm centre. Somebody left a tally on a stake: twelve cords. Not eight."},
					{"key": "track", "at": Vector2(130.0, 332.4), "name": "a cart-track", "text": "Wheels pressed deep, old, going one way: to the oak. Not away. The cart went in loaded and did not come out. A scatter of lamp-glass where the track bends, as if a lantern had been thrown."},
					{"key": "hob", "at": Vector2(132.4, 333.2), "name": "Hob's blazed tree", "text": "A blaze in the bark in a burner's hand, a stack and an arrow. HOB'S WAY TO THE KING. And under it, smaller, cut by a different knife, a child's: I WAS NOT AFRAID."},
				]},
			{"kind": "tracks", "r": 12.0, "label": "Hob's way to the oak",
				"text": "Follow the blazes to the Hollow King ({n}/{of})",
				"marks": [
					{"at": Vector2(142.0, 334.0), "text": "A blaze on a holly, the arrow bright with new sap, as if cut this week. But the bark has healed round it nine winters deep. It is only that the wood does not remember the years."},
					{"at": Vector2(154.0, 338.0), "text": "The trees grow strange here: all leaning one way, away, as if from a wind that never comes. Their roots are pulled up and over, in arches. Something has been walking beneath them."},
					{"at": Vector2(164.0, 340.0), "text": "A root as thick as a house, rising out of the ground and diving back in, and in its crook a lantern, unlit, hung by somebody tall. The glass is clean. It has been cleaned, every week."},
					{"at": Vector2(170.0, 342.0), "text": "The oak. You cannot see its crown. You see its trunk, sixteen yards round, and in it a doorway where firelight stands steady, and a smell of woodsmoke and cold leaves and something older."},
				]},
			{"kind": "find", "text": "Take a coal from the fire in the Hollow King's hall, in the lantern"},
			{"kind": "lantern_walk", "from": "oak_memory_coal", "to": Vector2(-140.0, 296.0), "r": 8.0, "label": "Hesper's farm",
				"relight": "Take another coal from the oak's hall fire.",
				"arrive": "You set the oak's ember in the farmhouse hearth. It takes the kindling at once, and for an instant the whole kitchen smells of leaves, and of a tree, and of being very, very old.",
				"text": "Carry the oak's ember west to Hesper's farm at Fallowmere. Walk it, the whole way: a run, a roll, a blow or deep water puts it out"},
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(-144.0, 298.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The farmhouse hearth",
				"text": "Read the farmhouse for what the family kept of the oak ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "cradle", "at": Vector2(-146.4, 299.6), "name": "a cradle of oak", "text": "A cradle in the loft, black with age, with a knot in its headboard like an eye. The Larks have rocked every one of their children in it. It is cut from a branch, Hesper says, of a tree she has never seen."},
					{"key": "gall", "at": Vector2(-144.0, 300.4), "name": "an oak-gall ink", "text": "A bottle of ink on the shelf made from the galls of the oak, the way her grandmother made it. The family Bible is written in it. The first line of the Bible is not scripture. It is: Remember the tree."},
					{"key": "rope", "at": Vector2(-141.6, 301.2), "name": "a rope of acorns", "text": "A rope of acorns over the door, one for each Lark. Nine winters old, the oldest, all dry, all rattling. Two are green: freshly strung, the cap still on."},
				]},
			{"kind": "vigil", "at": Vector2(-140.0, 294.0), "r": 9.0, "time": 60.0, "gloom": 0.6, "label": "The farmhouse door", "noun": "door", "prop": "lantern_lit",
				"waves": [{"at": 12.0, "kinds": ["husk"], "n": 2, "say": "The Southwood's dead come up the road to see where their oak's ember has gone."},
					{"at": 28.0, "kinds": ["wretch"], "n": 3, "say": "A burner in a soot-black coat stands at the gate and holds out his hands to the fire."},
					{"at": 44.0, "kinds": ["gaunt"], "n": 2, "say": "Something very tall leans over the hedge, and smells of leaves."}],
				"held": "The ember burns steady in the hearth. Beyond the hedge, a very long way south, a tree, you would swear, draws breath.", "away": "Go back to the farmhouse. A memory is kept in the house it was given to.",
				"text": "Keep the oak's ember in the farmhouse hearth through the night ({t} s)"},
			{"kind": "place", "text": "Decide what the oak's memory is for: leave a lantern in its hollow, bury a coal at the root of the oldest tree, or shut the hollow's door"},
			{"kind": "turnin", "who": "hesper", "text": "Tell Hesper what the count came to"},
		],
		"alt": {"oak": {7: "Tell Hesper a lantern burns in the oak"}, "root": {7: "Tell Hesper a coal is buried at her apple"}, "door": {7: "Tell Hesper the oak's door is shut"}},
