		"leaves": {"oak": {"at": Vector2(-140.0, 296.0), "prop": "lantern_lit"}, "root": {"at": Vector2(-140.0, 296.0), "prop": "slate"}, "door": {"at": Vector2(-140.0, 296.0), "prop": "mark"}},
		"outcome": {"oak": "Hesper listened with her eyes shut. 'A light in the hall,' she said. 'Where the cradle came from. I can see it.' She put her hand flat on the farmhouse table as if it were the oak itself. 'I did not know I had a tree to be homesick for.'",
			"root": "'The apple,' said Hesper, and laughed, and wiped her eyes on her apron. 'The oldest on the farm. Three weeks early.' She went out into the dark with a lantern to look at the tree, and came back with an apple blossom in her hair, though it was not the season, and did not say how.",
			"door": "'Shut.' Hesper nodded slowly. 'There are rooms in a family that are best shut. A room is not a grave.' She put the oak-gall ink away in its shelf and did not open the Bible again that night. In the morning there was a fresh acorn on the sill.",
			"": "The count was left as it was."}},
	"brine_road": {"name": "The Brine Road", "giver": "ardel", "zone": "saltpans", "offer": true, "avail": "qd:spire_coal",
		"where": "Ardel Wick, at Saltmarket",
		"text": "The carters of the brine road went home because of the quiet, not because of anything they saw: the pans give no sound and the salt makes no echo. Ardel Wick lit the Spire's lamp and answered the shut-out bell, and he has been sleeping better. He wants the road itself answered. Walk the brine road to the pans, take a salt-crusted lamp from the stranded ship, carry it all the way back to the Spire, and decide what a road is for when nobody drives it.",
		"steps": [
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(212.0, 84.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The brine road's head",
				"text": "Read the brine road's head for where the carters stopped ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "rut", "at": Vector2(209.6, 85.6), "name": "the carts' ruts", "text": "Two ruts, white with salt, running south to the pans in a long unbroken line, and one rut only, the east one, running back. The west one has not been used in nine winters. The salt has bridged it."},
					{"key": "chalk", "at": Vector2(212.0, 86.4), "name": "a carter's chalk", "text": "On a gatepost, a carter's tally: 40 TO THE PANS, 40 BACK. And under the last stroke, in someone else's chalk, newer: 39. I AM STILL COUNTING."},
					{"key": "shoe", "at": Vector2(214.4, 87.2), "name": "a mended shoe", "text": "A shoe on a stake at the road's head, mended with salt-cord, with a name in the tongue: NELLA CRAKE'S MOTHER. She walked this road every week for forty years, and someone sets her shoe on the stake each spring, and it is always dry."},
				]},
			{"kind": "tracks", "r": 12.0, "label": "The carters' road",
				"text": "Walk the brine road to the pans ({n}/{of})",
				"marks": [
					{"at": Vector2(212.0, 112.0), "text": "A cart-wheel, a good one, upright in the verge, white with salt to the hub. A carter's lamp hangs on its spoke, glass whole, wick dry. Somebody was meant to come back and take the wheel off."},
					{"at": Vector2(212.0, 148.0), "text": "A mile-stake with 20 cut in it. The salt has risen round its foot in a little white skirt. The wind has the sound of a very long exhale, and no one is breathing it."},
					{"at": Vector2(212.0, 176.0), "text": "The pans begin: great flat plates of white, and beyond them the sky, and no sound. You say your own name aloud and it does not come back. You say it again. It does not come back."},
					{"at": Vector2(214.0, 194.0), "text": "A great dark shape in the pans: a ship, heeled and stranded, forty-four yards of it on the salt. Its stern lamp is out. A rope-ladder hangs from its side, and the rungs are white with salt, and one of them is wet."},
				]},
			{"kind": "find", "text": "Take a coal from the Salt Ship's stern-lantern, in the lantern"},
			{"kind": "lantern_walk", "from": "brine_road_coal", "to": Vector2(242.0, 15.0), "r": 8.0, "label": "The Lamplighters' Spire",
				"relight": "Take another coal from the ship's stern-lantern.",
				"arrive": "You carry the ship's coal up the Spire's fourteen flights and set it in the lamp, and the lake, below, takes the light and gives it back. For a moment the shut-out bell at the Spire's foot, sounds, very quietly, in the breeze.",
				"text": "Carry the ship's coal north the whole length of the brine road to the Spire's lamp. Walk it: a run, a roll, a blow or deep water puts it out"},
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(242.0, 13.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The Spire's foot",
				"text": "Read the Spire's foot for what the pans have to do with the lamp ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "bell", "at": Vector2(239.6, 14.6), "name": "the shut-out bell", "text": "The eighth bell at the Spire's foot, facing the dark. The Founder's own hand is cut in its shoulder. The salt has crept up the stair in a thin white line, from the south: the pans want to come to the lamp."},
					{"key": "log", "at": Vector2(242.0, 15.4), "name": "the lamplighter's log", "text": "The lamplighter's log, open: THE SHIP CAME IN ON THE FIRST NIGHT. NOBODY BROUGHT HER. THE SALT PUSHED HER HERE, A MILE A WINTER. SHE IS COMING TO THE LAMP. I DO NOT KNOW WHAT SHE WANTS."},
					{"key": "shutter", "at": Vector2(244.4, 16.2), "name": "a half-closed shutter", "text": "The lamp's shutter, half closed, set that way by a lamplighter's hand, and left. A pale line of salt on the sill, the width of a finger, running up it to the glass. It is a road, in miniature."},
				]},
			{"kind": "vigil", "at": Vector2(242.0, 14.0), "r": 9.0, "time": 60.0, "gloom": 0.6, "label": "The Spire's foot", "noun": "spire", "prop": "lantern_lit",
				"waves": [{"at": 12.0, "kinds": ["wretch"], "n": 2, "say": "The pans send up what they have kept in the quiet."},
					{"at": 28.0, "kinds": ["husk"], "n": 3, "say": "The salt-dead come up the road in their dozens, white to the knees."},
					{"at": 44.0, "kinds": ["gaunt"], "n": 2, "say": "A very small light from the south steps closer, step by step, and does not go out."}],
				"held": "The Spire's lamp holds. The line of salt on the stair stops, a hand's breadth from the lamp, and does not creep.", "away": "Go back to the Spire. A road is answered at its far end.",
				"text": "Keep the ship's coal burning at the Spire through the night ({t} s)"},
			{"kind": "place", "text": "Decide what the road is for: open the Spire's shutter wide, leave it half closed, or strew salt on the stair"},
			{"kind": "turnin", "who": "ardel", "text": "Tell Ardel what the count came to"},
		],
		"alt": {"lamp": {7: "Tell Ardel the shutter is open"}, "half": {7: "Tell Ardel the shutter stays half closed"}, "salt": {7: "Tell Ardel the salt went back"}},
		"reward": {"ash": 40, "items": {"relic_fragment": 2, "ember_shard": 1}},
		"choose": [{"set": "kindler", "slot": "lantern", "rarity": 3}, {"set": "bell", "slot": "focus", "rarity": 3}, {"set": "tally", "slot": "girdle", "rarity": 3}],
		"leaves": {"lamp": {"at": Vector2(241.0, 15.0), "prop": "lantern_lit"}, "half": {"at": Vector2(241.0, 15.0), "prop": "lantern"}, "salt": {"at": Vector2(241.0, 15.0), "prop": "slabs"}},
		"outcome": {"lamp": "Ardel stood at the Saltmarket window with his back to you. 'Open,' he said. 'A lamp should not be rationed.' The light came across the lake onto his face. 'I have waited nine winters to be told that by someone who was not me.'",
			"half": "'Half.' Ardel nodded slowly. 'The lamplighter's own setting. I had thought it was a mistake.' He looked out. 'It was not. It was a measure. A road wants a lamp that it can afford.' He did not close the window.",
			"salt": "'You sent it back.' Ardel's mouth did something. 'The pans have waited a long time for somebody to return what they gave. A road is a thing you lend a place.' He took a pinch of the salt you had brought and put it in his tea, and said it was the best he had ever tasted.",
			"": "The count was left as it was."}},
	"arches_keeper": {"name": "The Arches' Last Page", "giver": "penn", "zone": "deepsouth", "offer": true, "avail": "qd:ds_door_castellum|qd:ds_water_road",
		"where": "Reeve Penn, in the tithe barn's porch at Fallowmere",
		"text": "The water-keeper wrote LIT IT ANYWAY on his last page and nobody has found out what came after it. The Long Arches carry nothing now, and Penn, who keeps sums, cannot bear a column that does not close. He wants the keeper's whole story: the beacon's foot, the dry channel to the castellum, a coal from the castellum's cresset carried back, and a decision about what the aqueduct is for now it does not hold water.",
		"steps": [
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(40.0, 249.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The Arches Beacon",
				"text": "Read the Arches Beacon for the keeper's first pages ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "page", "at": Vector2(37.6, 250.6), "name": "the keeper's first page", "text": "A page nailed to the beacon's post: THE WATER STOPPED ON THE NIGHT. I WALKED THE CHANNEL TO FIND THE BLOCKAGE. THERE WAS NONE. IT HAD STOPPED, THAT WAS ALL, LIKE A MAN HOLDING HIS BREATH."},
					{"key": "arch", "at": Vector2(40.0, 251.4), "name": "a counted arch", "text": "A tally cut in the keystone of the nearest arch: 4,011. The keeper counted every arch he walked beneath, every week, and the number never changed, and he never stopped counting."},
					{"key": "cup", "at": Vector2(42.4, 252.2), "name": "a keeper's cup", "text": "A pewter cup on the beacon's sill, full of rainwater, nine winters old and perfectly clear. The rain that fell in it did not wet the rim. It does not evaporate. It is, you gather, the last of the water."},
				]},
			{"kind": "tracks", "r": 12.0, "label": "The dry channel",
				"text": "Follow the dry channel under the arches to the castellum ({n}/{of})",
				"marks": [
					{"at": Vector2(20.0, 268.0), "text": "The channel below the arches, a stone trough, scoured white, with a thin dark line down its floor where the last water ran. The line is dry, but the stone near it is cooler than the stone round it."},
					{"at": Vector2(0.0, 290.0), "text": "A repair, fresh: new mortar, grey against old, laid in nine winters ago in one careful night. Someone was mending the channel when the water stopped, and finished the course before he left."},
					{"at": Vector2(-30.0, 318.0), "text": "A broken lamp-bracket in the arch's side, and under it, the lamp: whole, bright, a lamp that was lit and put out and lit and has not been touched. The wick is trimmed square."},
					{"at": Vector2(-52.0, 340.0), "text": "The castellum rises ahead, a squat water-tower with a great wheel on its flank and a dark cresset at its crown. A stair of forty steps climbs its side. Somebody has swept the steps. Somebody still does."},
				]},
			{"kind": "find", "text": "Take a coal from the castellum's cresset, in the lantern"},
			{"kind": "lantern_walk", "from": "arches_keeper_coal", "to": Vector2(40.0, 252.0), "r": 8.0, "label": "The Arches Beacon",
				"relight": "Take another coal from the castellum's cresset.",
				"arrive": "You lay the castellum's coal in the beacon's basket, and the beacon, which has burned nine winters on brushwood, takes it and burns whiter. Under the arches, very faintly, something that is not water moves along the channel.",
				"text": "Carry the castellum's coal north-east under the arches, back to the beacon. Walk it, the whole length of the channel: a run, a roll, a blow or deep water puts it out"},
			{"kind": "clues", "at": Vector2(44.0, 256.0), "r": 12.0, "need": 2, "label": "The Masons' Yard",
				"text": "Read the Masons' Yard for the arches' builders ({n}/{of} read)",
				"clues": [
					{"key": "mould", "at": Vector2(41.6, 257.6), "name": "the arch's mould", "text": "The wooden mould the first arch was built on, still standing in the yard, rotted to lace. The builders' marks are cut in it: each mason's own. The last mark is a water-drop."},
					{"key": "foreman", "at": Vector2(44.0, 258.4), "name": "the foreman's ledger", "text": "A ledger under a flat stone: THE ARCHES CARRY WATER TO THE FIELDS. THE FIELDS FEED THE ORDER. THE ORDER FEEDS NO ONE. I HAVE BUILT A THING THAT KEEPS ITS PROMISE TO THE WRONG MASTER."},
					{"key": "ring", "at": Vector2(46.4, 259.2), "name": "a ring of pebbles", "text": "A ring of pebbles, laid on the yard floor in the shape of an arch's plan, with a single white stone in the middle. Somebody sits in it. The pebbles are warm."},
				]},
			{"kind": "vigil", "at": Vector2(40.0, 250.0), "r": 9.0, "time": 60.0, "gloom": 0.6, "label": "The Arches Beacon", "noun": "beacon", "prop": "lantern_lit",
				"waves": [{"at": 12.0, "kinds": ["husk"], "n": 2, "say": "The dry channel remembers its water and sends up what lived in it."},
					{"at": 28.0, "kinds": ["wretch"], "n": 3, "say": "A water-keeper's dead stand along the arch-line like a row of pillars."},
					{"at": 44.0, "kinds": ["gaunt"], "n": 2, "say": "Water, very far below, moves once."}],
				"held": "The beacon burns white. Along the channel, from the castellum to the scarp, a very faint line of damp appears on the stone, and holds, and does not dry.", "away": "Go back to the beacon. An aqueduct is answered at its head.",
				"text": "Keep the castellum's coal burning at the Arches Beacon through the night ({t} s)"},
			{"kind": "place", "text": "Decide what the aqueduct is for: read the keeper's page aloud to the channel, pour his cup of rain into it, or count the arches"},
			{"kind": "turnin", "who": "penn", "text": "Tell Penn what the count came to"},
		],
		"alt": {"read": {7: "Tell Penn the page was read to the channel"}, "pour": {7: "Tell Penn the last water was poured"}, "count": {7: "Tell Penn the arches were counted"}},
		"reward": {"ash": 40, "items": {"relic_fragment": 2, "ember_shard": 1}},
		"choose": [{"set": "kindler", "slot": "lantern", "rarity": 3}, {"set": "bell", "slot": "focus", "rarity": 3}, {"set": "tally", "slot": "girdle", "rarity": 3}],
		"leaves": {"read": {"at": Vector2(42.0, 251.0), "prop": "lantern_lit"}, "pour": {"at": Vector2(42.0, 251.0), "prop": "slate"}, "count": {"at": Vector2(42.0, 251.0), "prop": "page"}},
		"outcome": {"read": "Penn stood in the barn's porch with his tally-stick and read the page himself, from memory, aloud. 'It may help someone find us,' he said. 'It did. It helped you.' He put the stick down and looked, for the first time in your hearing, quite pleased.",
			"pour": "'The last water,' said Penn quietly. 'Poured out. A sum closes when the last of the column is spent.' He rubbed his face. 'I did not think I would live to see the Arches carry anything. A thread, you say. A thread is more than I had.'",
			"count": "'Four thousand and twelve.' Penn wrote it in the reeve's book, in his best hand, and underlined it twice. 'One over. The first column I have seen in nine winters that did not close, and I am satisfied with it.' He tapped the page. 'An honest sum has a remainder.'",
			"": "The count was left as it was."}},
}

